12-6-27:
Beth-elThis city was originally assigned to Benjamin (Joshua 18:22), but later it
was incorporated into the northern kingdom as part of Ephraim. See on Gen. 28:19;
Joshua 18:22.

12-15-5:
ContinuallyHeb. tamid, a word employed in connection with the daily,
continuous services that were to be conducted in the sanctuary (see Ex. 25:30; 27:20;
29:38; 30:8; etc.).

12-26-17:
ElihuThis should probably be Eliab, the eldest son of Jesse (see 1 Sam. 16:6;
17:13, 28; 1 Chron. 2:13), unless he was “brother” in the sense of “relative” (see on ch.
2:7).
